### Current Step Rationale
This step focuses on setting up the user interface for the QR code generator. It involves creating the `index.html` file, incorporating DaisyUI for styling, and laying out the essential UI components such as the URL input, generate button, QR code display area, recent QR codes section, clear button, settings dropdown, and motivational message display.

### Plan for this Step
1. Create a new file `qr-code-generator/index.html`.
2. Add basic HTML5 structure.
3. Include DaisyUI CDN links in the `<head>` section.
4. Add the `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">` tag for responsiveness.
5. Create a main container using DaisyUI classes for centering and layout.
6. Implement a form with an `<input type="text">` for URL input and a "Generate" button using DaisyUI `btn` classes.
7. Add a `<div>` element with an `id` (e.g., `qrcode-container`) where the QR code canvas will be rendered.
8. Add a section for "Recent QR Codes" (e.g., a `<ul>` or `<div>` with an `id`).
9. Add a "Clear" button.
10. Add a "Settings" dropdown/modal for QR code parameters (e.g., size, error correction).
11. Add a `<div>` for displaying motivational messages.
12. Link to `script.js` at the end of the `<body>`.
